    `one room is used primarily for a business conducted primarily elsewhere`    IS FALSE
    `the land is used for another purpose or earns other income`                  IS FALSE

`vacant land` MEANS `The land and its use` WITH
    `is a strata lot or strata lots`                                              IS FALSE
    `the building is designed, constructed or adapted for residential purposes`  IS FALSE
    `number of lots`                                                              IS 1
    `the lots adjoin`                                                             IS FALSE
    `the lots are in the same ownership`                                          IS FALSE
    `the lots are a single residence`                                             IS FALSE
    `there is a residential occupancy other than the owner's`                     IS FALSE
    `that occupancy is one excluded residential occupancy`                        IS FALSE
    `that occupancy is on a lot the owner also lives on`                          IS FALSE
    `one room is used primarily for a business conducted primarily elsewhere`    IS FALSE
    `the land is used for another purpose or earns other income`                  IS FALSE

-- One owner (or co-owners who all live there), no company, trust or other family home.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `the land` IS A `The land and its use`, `the use` IS A `Use at the taxing date`
GIVETH A `Home at the taxing date`
`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` MEANS
    `Home at the taxing date` WITH
        `land tax year`                                                                  IS `the year`
        `the land`                                                                       IS `the land`
        `the use`                                                                        IS `the use`
        `a company owns or co-owns it, other than a trustee company or a trustee of a concessional trust` IS FALSE
        `the owners who live there are owners only as trustees`                          IS FALSE
        `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns it`                                IS FALSE
        `the family owns another residence one of them uses as a principal place of residence` IS FALSE
        `the family lodged an election in time`                                          IS FALSE
        `the family elected this residence`                                              IS FALSE
        `this residence has the highest land value of the family's residences`           IS FALSE
        `percentage owned by the owners who live there`                                  IS 100
        `the owner is a participant in an approved shared equity scheme`                 IS FALSE
        `the owner was previously entitled to the exemption for this land`               IS FALSE

-- The variations on ownership, family and interest (cl 11, 12, 15).
GIVEN `the year`     IS A NUMBER
      `company`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `special trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other home`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `elected`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `chose this`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `highest`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `percentage`   IS A NUMBER
      `shared equity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home at the taxing date`
`a lived-in house where` MEANS
    `Home at the taxing date` WITH
        `land tax year`                                                                  IS `the year`
        `the land`                                                                       IS `a house on one lot, used only as a home`
        `the use`                                                                        IS `the owner lives there` TRUE FALSE
        `a company owns or co-owns it, other than a trustee company or a trustee of a concessional trust` IS `company`
        `the owners who live there are owners only as trustees`                          IS FALSE
        `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns it`                                IS `special trust`
        `the family owns another residence one of them uses as a principal place of residence` IS `other home`
        `the family lodged an election in time`                                          IS `elected`
        `the family elected this residence`                                              IS `chose this`
        `this residence has the highest land value of the family's residences`           IS `highest`
        `percentage owned by the owners who live there`                                  IS `percentage`
        `the owner is a participant in an approved shared equity scheme`                 IS `shared equity`
        `the owner was previously entitled to the exemption for this land`               IS `before`

`living there since before 1 July` MEANS `the owner lives there` TRUE FALSE
`moved in after 1 July, not accepted` MEANS `the owner lives there` FALSE FALSE
`moved in after 1 July, accepted by the Chief Commissioner` MEANS `the owner lives there` FALSE TRUE

§§ `Schedule 1A cll 2-5, 13-14 -- living there`

-- cl 2(1)(a), (2)(a), cl 3: a house lived in since before 1 July, used only as a home: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 2(2): moved in after 1 July 2025; unless the Chief Commissioner is satisfied, not exempt for 2026.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` `moved in after 1 July, not accepted`) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` `moved in after 1 July, accepted by the Chief Commissioner`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 4(1)-(3): one let flat is disregarded, "even if income is derived": exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house with a let granny flat` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 3(1)(b), cl 4(1)(b): more than one excluded occupancy: not residential land.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house with two let flats` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `not exempt` `it is not a parcel of residential land or a strata lot`
-- cl 5: one room used for a business conducted elsewhere is disregarded: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house with one room as an office for a business run elsewhere` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 3(1): a shop is another purpose: not residential land.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house with a shop at the front` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `not exempt` `it is not a parcel of residential land or a strata lot`
-- cl 2(1)(b): a strata lot: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 13(1): 2 adjoining lots, same ownership, one residence: exempt; lots that do not adjoin: not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house across two adjoining lots` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house and a garden lot across the road` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `not exempt` `it is 2 or more lots that do not meet clause 13 or 14`
-- cl 4(4): on 2 lots the excluded occupancy must be on a lot the owner lives on.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `two adjoining lots with a let flat on the second` `living there since before 1 July`) EQUALS `not exempt` `it is not a parcel of residential land or a strata lot`
-- No use as a home at all.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` `none of these`) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`

§§ `Schedule 1A cll 11, 12, 15 -- who owns it, the family, and the 25 percent rule`

-- Arguments: year; company; special trust; other family home; election lodged; elected this; this highest; percentage
-- owned by those who live there; shared equity scheme; previously entitled.
-- cl 11(1)(a): a company co-owns it.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt` `clause 11 excludes land owned by a company or a trustee`
-- cl 11(1)(c): a trustee of a special trust co-owns it.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt` `clause 11 excludes land owned by a company or a trustee`
-- cl 12(2): the family elected its other home in time: this one is not the family's.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt` `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`
-- cl 12(2): the family elected this home: exempt (even though it is not the more valuable).
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 12(5): no election; this home has the highest land value: exempt; it does not: not exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt` `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`
-- cl 15(1): those who live there own 20%: not exempt; 25% is enough.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owners who live there own less than a 25 percent interest`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 25 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 15(2): an approved shared equity scheme participant with 20%: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- Schedule 2 cl 70: previously entitled, 20%: exempt for 2025; not for 2026 (finding 7).
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2025 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a lived-in house where` 2026 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owners who live there own less than a 25 percent interest`

§§ `Schedule 1A cl 6 -- building a home`

-- Noah bought a vacant block in 2023 and is building. cl 6(3)(a): the period is 2024 to 2027.
GIVEN `bought` IS A NUMBER, `someone lived there` IS A BOOLEAN, `they left` IS A NUMBER, `satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN, `period` IS A NUMBER, `income` IS A BOOLEAN, `other home` IS A BOOLEAN, `more than 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use at the taxing date`
`Noah building, where` MEANS
    `the owner is building a home there`
        (`Building facts` WITH
            `the land is unoccupied`                                                         IS TRUE
            `the owner intends to live there solely as principal place of residence`        IS TRUE
            `it is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out or is carrying out the works` IS TRUE
            `income has been derived since the works physically began`                       IS `income`
            `the intended use is unlawful`                                                   IS FALSE
            `the year the owner became the owner`                                            IS `bought`
            `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`      IS `someone lived there`
            `the year that person stopped living there`                                      IS `they left`
            `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the works began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year` IS `satisfied`
            `the period in tax years, as the Chief Commissioner has extended it`             IS `period`
            `the owner or a family member has other land counted as a principal place of residence` IS `other home`
            `the owner owns land outside NSW that is the principal place of residence of the owner or a family member` IS FALSE
            `the land could lawfully have more than 2 residences built on it`                IS `more than 2`)

-- Arguments: bought; someone else lived there; year they left; Chief Commissioner satisfied (cl 6(4)); period; income;
-- other home counted (cl 6(7)(a)); more than 2 residences (cl 6(7)(c)).
-- 2026 is inside 2024-2027: exempt. 2024, the first year: exempt. 2023, the year of purchase: not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2024 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2023 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- 2028 is outside 2024-2027: not exempt; with the period extended to 6 (cl 6(7A)), 2024-2029: exempt for 2028, not 2030.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2028 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2028 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 6 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2030 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 6 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 6(7A) allows "up to 6": an extension stated as 8 years is read as 6, so 2030 is still outside.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2030 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 8 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 6(2)(b): income since the works began; cl 6(7)(a): another home counted; cl 6(7)(c): room for more than 2 homes.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 6(3)(b), (4)(a): a tenant stayed until 2024; the period is 2025-2028. With the Chief Commissioner satisfied, exempt for
-- 2026; without, not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 TRUE 2024 TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 TRUE 2024 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- 2028 is the last year of 2025-2028: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2028 `vacant land` (`Noah building, where` 2023 TRUE 2024 TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`

-- cl 6(5): the move-in deadline is the end of the last tax year of the period.
-- Arguments: year became owner; someone else lived there; year they left; tax years allowed.
#ASSERT `By what date must I move into the home I am building` 2023 FALSE 0 4 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2027
#ASSERT `By what date must I move into the home I am building` 2023 FALSE 0 6 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2029
#ASSERT `By what date must I move into the home I am building` 2023 TRUE 2024 4 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2028
-- cl 6(5): then at least 6 months. 10 January 2028 + 6 months = 10 July 2028; 31 August 2027 + 6 months: February 2028
-- has 29 days, so 29 February 2028; 31 August 2028 + 6 months: 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `Until what date must I keep living in the home I built` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2028) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 7 2028
#ASSERT `Until what date must I keep living in the home I built` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2027) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `Until what date must I keep living in the home I built` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2028) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2029

§§ `Schedule 1A cl 7 -- moving home`

-- Priya lived in her Ryde house and bought a new home; the 2026 taxing date is 31 December 2025.
GIVEN `the day she bought the new home` IS A DATE, `former home earned other income` IS A BOOLEAN, `claimed before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use at the taxing date`
`Priya moving, where` MEANS
    `the owner is moving home`
        (`Moving facts` WITH
            `the owner owns both a former residence and a new residence`                     IS TRUE
            `the former residence was the owner's principal place of residence on this or the preceding taxing date` IS TRUE
            `the new residence is being or is intended to be the owner's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
            `the former residence was used only as the owner's home, without other income, since the preceding 1 July` IS (NOT `former home earned other income`)
            `the day the owner became the owner of the new residence`                        IS `the day she bought the new home`
            `the new residence was used only as the owner's home or by a tenant of the previous owner` IS TRUE
            `both residences were already exempt under clause 7 on an earlier taxing date`  IS `claimed before`)

-- cl 7(2)(b): bought 15 September 2025, within 6 months before 31 December 2025: both homes exempt for 2026.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Priya moving, where` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- Bought 1 July 2025: inside (the reading of "6 months before"); 30 June 2025: outside.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Priya moving, where` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Priya moving, where` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2025) FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 7(2)(a): the former home was let to someone other than the buyer since 1 July: not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Priya moving, where` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 7(3): not for more than one taxing date.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Priya moving, where` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 7(3A): she must be living in the new home by the next taxing date, 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must I be living in my new home` 2026 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2026

§§ `Schedule 1A cl 8 -- living away`

-- Tom lived in his Newcastle unit for 3 years and left on 1 March 2021. cl 8(2): 6 years from then is 1 March 2027.
GIVEN `left` IS A DATE, `six months first` IS A BOOLEAN, `other home` IS A BOOLEAN, `care days` IS A NUMBER, `income` IS A BOOLEAN, `long letting` IS A BOOLEAN, `days let` IS A NUMBER, `cost recovery` IS A BOOLEAN, `unfit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use at the taxing date`
`Tom away, where` MEANS
    `the owner is away`
        (`Absence facts` WITH
            `the owner lived there as principal place of residence continuously for at least 6 months` IS `six months first`
            `the owner owns other land the owner lives in as principal place of residence` IS `other home`
            `the day the owner stopped living there`                                         IS `left`
            `days in full time care since then`                                              IS `care days`
            `income was derived from the land in the preceding tax year`                     IS `income`
            `a right of occupation in that year ran continuously for more than 6 months`     IS `long letting`
            `days of occupation let in that year`                                            IS `days let`
            `the income was no more than rates, charges and maintenance costs`               IS `cost recovery`
            `the land has been incapable of being used as a residence for more than 4 years` IS `unfit`)

`1 March 2021` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2021

-- Arguments: left; lived 6 months first; owns another home he lives in; days in full time care; income in the preceding
-- year; a letting over 6 months; days let; cost recovery only; unfit for over 4 years.
-- 2026 (31 December 2025 is before 1 March 2027), no income: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 8(7)(a): short lets totalling 150 days, none over 6 months: exempt. 200 days: over 182, not exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 150 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE 200 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- A 12-month lease runs continuously for more than 6 months: not exempt (finding 6).
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 365 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 8(7)(b): the same lease at a rent that only covers rates, charges and maintenance: exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE 365 TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 8(2): 2028 (31 December 2027 is after 1 March 2027): not exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2028 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 8(4): 365 days in full time care push the end to 29 February 2028 (1 March 2027 + 365 days, 2028 being a leap year):
-- exempt for 2028.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2028 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 365 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `Until what date can my former home be treated as my home` `1 March 2021` 0 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `Until what date can my former home be treated as my home` `1 March 2021` 365 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028
-- cl 8(1)(b): he owns another home he lives in; cl 8(1)(a): he lived there less than 6 months; cl 8(3A): unfit for over
-- 4 years: not exempt.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a strata apartment` (`Tom away, where` `1 March 2021` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`

§§ `Schedule 1A cl 9 -- after the owner's death`

-- Margaret lived in her Wollongong house until she died on 15 March 2024. cl 9(2)(a): 2 years, to 15 March 2026.
GIVEN `transferred` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended to` IS A DATE, `lived there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use at the taxing date`
`Margaret's estate, where` MEANS
    `the owner has died`
        (`Death facts` WITH
            `immediately before death the owner owned the land and lived there as principal place of residence` IS `lived there`
            `the day the owner died`                                                         IS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2024
            `the land has been transferred to someone other than the personal representative or a beneficiary` IS `transferred`
            `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`                     IS `extended`
            `the day the extended period ends`                                               IS `extended to`)

-- Arguments: transferred to an outsider; extended; extended to; she lived there immediately before death.
-- 2025 (31 December 2024) and 2026 (31 December 2025): within 2 years: exempt. 2027 (31 December 2026): not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2025 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) TRUE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) TRUE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2027 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) TRUE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
-- cl 9(3): extended in writing to 30 June 2027: exempt for 2027.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2027 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027) TRUE)) EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- cl 9(2)(b): sold to a buyer: not; cl 9(1): she did not live there: not.
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) TRUE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
#ASSERT `the principal place of residence exemption for` (`a home its owner-occupiers own outright` 2026 `a house on one lot, used only as a home` (`Margaret's estate, where` FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026) FALSE)) EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`

§§ `The seat's home questions, asked directly`

-- The same facts through each exported question, to check that the seat wires its answers into the core.
-- Shared arguments: year; strata; building; lots; adjoin; same owners; single home; other occupancy; excluded; on my lot;
-- business room; other use; company; trustee only; special trust; other family home; election; elected this; highest;
-- percentage; shared equity; previously entitled.

-- Mia lives in her Parramatta house, as since before 1 July 2025: exempt for 2026.
`Mia asks about 2026` MEANS `Is my home exempt while I live in it` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Mia asks about 2026` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- Mia lets her granny flat (one excluded occupancy): still exempt.
`Mia with a let granny flat` MEANS `Is my home exempt while I live in it` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Mia with a let granny flat` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- Mia and her husband also own a holiday house his family uses as its home; no election; the holiday house is worth more.
`Mia with a family second home` MEANS `Is my home exempt while I live in it` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Mia with a family second home` EQUALS `not exempt` `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`

-- Noah's block, 2026, bought 2023, through the building question: exempt.
`Noah asks about 2026` MEANS `Is my land exempt while I build my home` 2026 FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2023 FALSE 0 FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Noah asks about 2026` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`

-- Priya, 2026, bought the new home on 15 September 2025: exempt.
`Priya asks about 2026` MEANS `Are both my homes exempt in the year I move` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Priya asks about 2026` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
-- Priya's family also owns a third home her husband lives in, and has not elected; it is worth more: cl 12 applies to it.
`Priya with a third home` MEANS `Are both my homes exempt in the year I move` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Priya with a third home` EQUALS `not exempt` `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`

-- Tom, 2026, away since 1 March 2021, 150 days of short lets in 2025: exempt.
`Tom asks about 2026` MEANS `Is my former home still exempt while I am away` 2026 TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 March 2021` 0 TRUE FALSE 150 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Tom asks about 2026` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`

-- Margaret's executor, 2026: exempt.
`Margaret's executor asks about 2026` MEANS `Is the home of the owner who died still exempt` 2026 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2024) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Margaret's executor asks about 2026` EQUALS `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
`Margaret's executor asks about 2027` MEANS `Is the home of the owner who died still exempt` 2027 FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2024) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Margaret's executor asks about 2027` EQUALS `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`

§§ `s 12 and Schedule 1A cl 12 -- the return and the family election`

-- s 12(1A)-(1B): for 2026, by 31 January 2026, listing the land owned at midnight on 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a land tax return` 2026 TRUE EQUALS `I must lodge a land tax return` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2025)
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a land tax return` 2026 FALSE EQUALS `no Gazette order requires me to lodge a return for the year, though the Chief Commissioner may ask for one under s 12(2)`
-- cl 12(3)-(4): served 10 February 2026; with a 60-day objection period (a test input; s 89 is not deposited): 10 February
-- + 60 days = 11 April 2026 (18 days to 28 February, 31 in March, 11 in April).
#ASSERT `By what date must my family lodge its election` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) 60 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 4 2026

§§ `ss 39 and 40 -- paying`

-- s 39(3): served 10 February 2026; the notice says 1 March 2026 (19 days); not earlier than 30 days: 12 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must I pay my land tax` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 12 3 2026
-- s 39(1): the notice says 31 March 2026, later than 30 days: 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By what date must I pay my land tax` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026
-- s 40: assessed 2,000; a 1.5% rate (a test input: the Treasurer's order is not deposited). Paid in full on 5 March 2026 (23
-- days after service), nothing else owing: 2,000 x 1.5% = 30. On 12 March (30 days): 30. On 13 March (31 days): 0.
#ASSERT `What early payment discount do I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 3 2026) TRUE TRUE 2000 1.5 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `What early payment discount do I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 3 2026) TRUE TRUE 2000 1.5 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `What early payment discount do I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 13 3 2026) TRUE TRUE 2000 1.5 EQUALS 0
-- s 40(1)(a): part paid: 0. s 40(1)(b): other land tax owing and not paid with it: 0.
#ASSERT `What early payment discount do I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 3 2026) FALSE TRUE 2000 1.5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What early payment discount do I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 3 2026) TRUE FALSE 2000 1.5 EQUALS 0

§§ `Land Tax Act ss 5A and 5B -- surcharge for a foreign person`

-- Arguments: year; foreign person; value of interests in residential land not exempt from surcharge; other use.
-- s 5A(2)(d): 31 December 2025 is "any other year, commencing with 2024": 5% of 800,000 = 40,000 for 2026, and for 2025.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 40000
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2025 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 40000
-- s 5A(2)(c): 31 December 2022 and 2023 (the 2023 and 2024 land tax years): 4% of 800,000 = 32,000 (finding 2).
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2024 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 32000
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2023 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 32000
-- s 5A(2)(b): 31 December 2017-2021 (2018-2022): 2% = 16,000. (a): 31 December 2016 (2017): 0.75% = 6,000.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2022 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 16000
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2018 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 16000
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2017 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 6000
-- Before 2017, s 5A levies nothing; a person who is not foreign owes none.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2016 TRUE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2026 FALSE 800000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
-- s 5A(4)(d): partly used for other purposes: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE 800000 TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `residential land partly used for other purposes needs the Duties Act 1997 s 104ZB apportionment factor, not deposited`
-- s 5A(3), (4)(h): Wei, a foreign person, owns a 900,000 investment flat alone, 2026. Ordinary land tax: under the
-- 1,075,000 threshold, nil. Surcharge: no threshold, 5% x 900,000 = 45,000, payable even though no land tax is.
#ASSERT `How much land tax do I owe` 2026 900000 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` (`Land tax assessed` WITH `taxable value on the separate assessment` IS 900000, `payable on the separate assessment` IS 0, `payable on the joint assessments` IS 0)
#ASSERT `How much surcharge land tax do I owe` 2026 TRUE 900000 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 45000

-- s 5B(1). Arguments: home exempt under Schedule 1A; permanent resident at the 31 December; the Chief Commissioner
-- satisfied of the intention; declaration lodged with a required return; retirement visa holder.
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 5BA(1): a retirement visa holder: the Regulation's modifications are needed: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my home exempt from surcharge land tax` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `the answer depends on the Land Tax Management Regulation 2024, which is not deposited`

-- s 5B(2): 200 continuous days ending by 31 December: start by 15 June (16 days in June + 31 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 =
-- 200), in a leap year too, since February is before June.
#ASSERT `By what date must I start my 200 days` 2026 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2026
#ASSERT `By what date must I start my 200 days` 2028 EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2028
-- 1 March to 30 September 2026: 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 30 = 214 days: met. 1 June to 15 December: 30 + 31 + 31 +
-- 30 + 31 + 30 + 15 = 198: not met. 15 June to 31 December: 200: met; 16 June: 199: not.
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 12 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 16 6 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- Only the days inside the land tax year count: 1 December 2025 to 30 June 2026 gives 181 days in 2026 (31 + 28 + 31 + 30
-- + 31 + 30): not met; 1 December 2025 to 31 August 2026 gives 243: met.
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I meet the 200-day residence requirement` 2026 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2026) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Regulative rules -- traces`

-- s 12(1A)-(1B), 2026. Day 0 is 1 January 2026; 31 January is day 30.
#ASSERT `days from 1 January to the s 12(1A) return date` 2026 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12(1A)-(1B) -- a person a Gazette order covers must lodge a land tax return by 31 January` 2026 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner` `furnish a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on 31 December` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12(1A)-(1B) -- a person a Gazette order covers must lodge a land tax return by 31 January` 2026 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner` `furnish a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on 31 December` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 12(1A)-(1B) -- a person a Gazette order covers must lodge a land tax return by 31 January` 2026 FALSE) 0 EMPTY EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the owner, "s 12(1A)-(1B): ..." (the return lodged on 1 February, day 31)
#TRACE `s 12(1A)-(1B) -- a person a Gazette order covers must lodge a land tax return by 31 January` 2026 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `furnish a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on 31 December` AT 31

-- Schedule 1A cl 12(2)-(5), with a 60-day objection period (a test input). Day 0 is service of the first notice.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Schedule 1A cl 12(2)-(5) -- the family may elect its principal place of residence within the objection period` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the members of the family` `lodge a written election of the family's principal place of residence` 20), (EVENT `the Chief Commissioner` `treat the elected residence as the family's principal place of residence` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Lodged on day 61, too late: the residence with the highest land value is treated as the family's.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Schedule 1A cl 12(2)-(5) -- the family may elect its principal place of residence within the objection period` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the members of the family` `lodge a written election of the family's principal place of residence` 61), (EVENT `the Chief Commissioner` `treat the residence with the highest land value as the family's principal place of residence` 70)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Chief Commissioner's obligation to treat the elected residence still pending (an election was lodged in time,
-- so treating the highest-valued residence instead does not settle it)
#TRACE `Schedule 1A cl 12(2)-(5) -- the family may elect its principal place of residence within the objection period` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the members of the family` DOES `lodge a written election of the family's principal place of residence` AT 20
    PARTY `the Chief Commissioner` DOES `treat the residence with the highest land value as the family's principal place of residence` AT 45

-- Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6): 400 days to the end of the period; 182 days in the 6 months after moving in.
-- Moves in on day 300 and stays past day 481 (300 + 181): FULFILLED.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6) -- to keep the building exemption the owner must move in by the end of the period and stay 6 months` 400 182) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner` `begin actually using and occupying the land as principal place of residence` 300), (EVENT `the owner` `stop using and occupying the land as principal place of residence` 482)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the owner, "Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6): the owner did not keep living there for 6 months; ..." (left on day 400)
#TRACE `Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6) -- to keep the building exemption the owner must move in by the end of the period and stay 6 months` 400 182 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `begin actually using and occupying the land as principal place of residence` AT 300
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `stop using and occupying the land as principal place of residence` AT 400
-- expect: BREACH BY the owner, "Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6): the owner did not move in by the end of the clause 6 period; ..."
#TRACE `Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6) -- to keep the building exemption the owner must move in by the end of the period and stay 6 months` 400 182 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 401)

-- Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4), 2026: day 0 is 31 December 2025; the next taxing date is day 365.
#ASSERT `days from the taxing date to the next taxing date for` 2026 EQUALS 365
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4) -- to keep both exemptions the owner must be living in the new residence by the next taxing date` 2026) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner` `begin actually using and occupying the new residence as principal place of residence` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the owner, "Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4): ..." (not living in the new residence by 31 December 2026)
#TRACE `Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4) -- to keep both exemptions the owner must be living in the new residence by the next taxing date` 2026 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)

-- s 39(1), (3). Day 0 is service. The notice says 45 days: paid on day 45, FULFILLED. The notice says 14 days: 30 apply,
-- paid on day 30, FULFILLED.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 39(1), (3) -- the taxpayer must pay by the due date in the notice, which is not earlier than 30 days after service` 45) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the land tax assessed` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 39(1), (3) -- the taxpayer must pay by the due date in the notice, which is not earlier than 30 days after service` 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the land tax assessed` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 39(1), (3): ..." (paid on day 46 of 45)
#TRACE `s 39(1), (3) -- the taxpayer must pay by the due date in the notice, which is not earlier than 30 days after service` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `pay the land tax assessed` AT 46

-- s 40. Day 0 is service. Paid in full on day 20; the discount allowed on day 25: FULFILLED. Paid on day 31: no discount,
-- and no breach: FULFILLED. Other tax owing: nothing to earn: FULFILLED.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- paying the whole amount within 30 days of service earns the discount` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the whole amount specified in the assessment` 20), (EVENT `the Chief Commissioner` `allow the early payment discount` 25)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- paying the whole amount within 30 days of service earns the discount` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the whole amount specified in the assessment` 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 40 -- paying the whole amount within 30 days of service earns the discount` FALSE) 0 EMPTY EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Chief Commissioner's obligation to allow the discount still pending (paid on day 20, no discount yet)
#TRACE `s 40 -- paying the whole amount within 30 days of service earns the discount` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `pay the whole amount specified in the assessment` AT 20

-- Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4), 2026. Day 0 is 1 January 2026; 31 December is day 364. Starting on 15 June 2026 (day 165), the
-- 200th day is day 364: FULFILLED, consistent with the start-by date above.
#ASSERT `days from 1 January to 31 December of` 2026 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT `days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) `to` (`By what date must I start my 200 days` 2026) PLUS 199 EQUALS 364
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4) -- a foreign person exempt from surcharge on the home must live there 200 continuous days in the year` 2026) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the foreign person` `complete 200 days of continuous use and occupation as principal place of residence` 364)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4) -- a foreign person exempt from surcharge on the home must live there 200 continuous days in the year` 2026) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the foreign person` `complete 200 days of continuous use and occupation as principal place of residence` 300)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the foreign person, "Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4): ..." (no 200-day stretch by 31 December 2026)
#TRACE `Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4) -- a foreign person exempt from surcharge on the home must live there 200 continuous days in the year` 2026 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 365)
